questions.explanation:
The word doing the work is **programmatically**, across **15 tables**, driven by a naming convention. **Tabular Editor** has a **C# scripting** engine over the Tabular Object Model, so the whole job is a short loop:

```csharp
foreach (var c in Model.AllColumns.Where(c => c.Name.EndsWith("Key"))) {
    c.IsHidden        = true;
    c.IsNullable     = false;
    c.SummarizeBy     = AggregateFunction.None;
    c.IsAvailableInMDX = false;
    c.IsKey           = true;
}
```

Those five lines are the five bullet points in the question, one for one.

- **A Power BI Desktop** – every property is there in the Properties pane, but you would set them by hand, column by column, across 15 tables. Not programmatic.
- **B ALM Toolkit** – *compares and deploys* differences between two models. It does not author property changes.
- **D DAX Studio** – queries and profiles a model; it is read-only against model metadata.

